UR  - https://www.sciencedirect.com/science/article/pii/S0952197625031689
KW  - Stochastic configuration networks
KW  - Randomized learning
KW  - Industrial artificial intelligence
AB  - Stochastic configuration networks (SCNs) are a class of randomized learner models that have recently attracted increasing attention due to the possibility of fast and low-cost implementation in embedded systems. The two main operations in the algorithm are matrix multiplications and computation of the pseudoinverse for the hidden layer output matrix. However, these operations can be quite time-consuming for large-scale datasets and/or large numbers of neurons. This paper aims to accelerate the learning process of SCN. First, we propose a QR-update based pseudoinversion scheme that reduces the asymptotic complexity of the algorithm. Secondly, it is proposed to relax the inequality check at early iterations in order to reduce the size of the matrices to be multiplied. Empirical results on four different datasets demonstrate the efficiency and effectiveness of the proposed method to speed up SCN-based algorithms for use in industrial applications.
